      "final_text": "## Setup\n\n5557 is prime, and 8432 in binary is `10000011110000`, i.e.\n\n$$8432 = 2^{13} + 2^7 + 2^6 + 2^5 + 2^4$$\n\n## Repeated squaring of 7 (mod 5557)\n\n| Power | Computation | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| $7^1$ | \u2014 | 7 |\n| $7^2$ | $7^2$ | 49 |\n| $7^4$ | $49^2 = 2401$ | 2401 |\n| $7^8$ | $2401^2 = 5{,}764{,}801 = 1037\\cdot5557 + 2192$ | 2192 |\n| $7^{16}$ | $2192^2 = 4{,}804{,}864 = 864\\cdot5557 + 3616$ | 3616 |\n| $7^{32}$ | $3616^2 = 13{,}075{,}456 = 2352\\cdot5557 + 5392$ | 5392 ($\\equiv -165$) |\n| $7^{64}$ | $(-165)^2 = 27{,}225 = 4\\cdot5557 + 4997$ | 4997 ($\\equiv -560$) |\n| $7^{128}$ | $(-560)^2 = 313{,}600 = 56\\cdot5557 + 2408$ | 2408 |\n| $7^{256}$ | $2408^2 = 5{,}798{,}464 = 1043\\cdot5557 + 2513$ | 2513 |\n| $7^{512}$ | $2513^2 = 6{,}315{,}169 = 1136\\cdot5557 + 2417$ | 2417 |\n| $7^{1024}$ | $2417^2 = 5{,}841{,}889 = 1051\\cdot5557 + 1482$ | 1482 |\n| $7^{2048}$ | $1482^2 = 2{,}196{,}324 = 395\\cdot5557 + 1309$ | 1309 |\n| $7^{4096}$ | $1309^2 = 1{,}713{,}481 = 308\\cdot5557 + 1925$ | 1925 |\n| $7^{8192}$ | $1925^2 = 3{,}705{,}625 = 666\\cdot5557 + 4663$ | 4663 |\n\n## Combining the selected factors\n\nMultiply the terms for bits 13, 7, 6, 5, 4 \u2014 that is $4663 \\cdot 2408 \\cdot 4997 \\cdot 5392 \\cdot 3616$:\n\n- $4663 \\cdot 2408 = 11{,}228{,}504 \\equiv 3364$\n- $3364 \\cdot 4997 \\equiv 3364 \\cdot(-560) = -1{,}883{,}840 \\equiv -17 \\equiv 5540$\n- $5540 \\cdot 5392 \\equiv (-17)(-165) = 2805$\n- $2805 \\cdot 3616 = 10{,}142{,}880 \\equiv 1355$\n\n**Check:** since 5557 is prime, Fermat's little theorem gives $8432 \\bmod 5556 = 2876$, and recomputing $7^{2876}$ from the same square table ($2048{+}512{+}256{+}32{+}16{+}8{+}4$) also yields 1355.\n\n**1355**"
